# OsUpdateActivity v1 — OOBE update phase (D-310, report 3a2207978e4c, 2026-10-01).
# Posted by WindowsUpdateWatcherHost (CollectorConfiguration.OobeUpdatePhaseMode Shadow or Active)
# for every step of a Windows/.NET update: the Windows Update client on the System/Operational
# logs (source "wu": download_started, downloaded, install_started, installed, failed) and the
# CBS servicing steps on the Setup log (source "servicing": staging_started, staged,
# install_started, reboot_required, installed, failed). Store, Defender and other updates never
# post it. Payload: step (mandatory), source, update (title or KB).
# Reducer: HandleOsUpdateActivityV1 → records DecisionState.OsUpdateFacts (event-time ordered);
# the earliest activity after the ESP exit while no real user signed in anchors the OOBE update
# phase (PostExitActivityUtc). The phase holds the AdvisoryCompletion deadline within its own
# bounds: 3 h while the update runs (then Failed oobe_update_not_finished), 60 min for the
# sign-in after it ended (then the engine stops waiting — StoppedWaitingReason, no verdict).
# No stage change, no deadline. A signal without a step is a dead end.
